## Press-On and At-Home Day of the Dead Nail Options

Day of the dead press-on nails typically last one to two weeks with proper application, and can stretch closer to three weeks with strong adhesive tabs or nail glue combined with minimal early water exposure. That timeline puts press-ons squarely between a DIY polish manicure and a full gel or acrylic set in terms of both durability and commitment.

This category has grown considerably, and it now covers nearly the full visual range already discussed, sugar skulls, Catrina portraits, marigold florals, papel picado borders, in pre-made sets ready to apply without any painting at all. For anyone who wants a specific, detailed look without the time investment or skill curve of hand-painting, press-ons close that gap entirely.

Application quality matters more than the design itself when it comes to how long these sets actually hold. Proper nail prep, pushing back cuticles, lightly buffing the natural nail surface, and cleaning away oils before application, does more for longevity than the adhesive brand or the polish formula underneath it. Sizing each nail correctly, rather than forcing a close-enough fit, prevents the lifting that ends most press-on sets early.

