## Choosing a Direction Worth Trying

None of this needs to be an either-or decision. A short almond set with one hand-painted marigold accent nail belongs in the same category as a full coffin set covered in Catrina portraits, both are day of the dead nails, both draw from the same well of symbols, and both are equally valid starting points.

The through-line across every style covered here is intention. The color choices, the symbols, the way a marigold petal or a calavera's floral crown gets rendered, all of it carries meaning beyond decoration. That is what separates this aesthetic from a generic fall nail trend, and it is worth carrying into whatever direction feels most appealing.

Whether the plan is booking a salon appointment with a reference photo in hand or spending a Friday night with a dotting tool and a bottle of orange polish, there is a specific style above worth trying this year, not just saving for later.
